  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Salis beach is a long sandy beach at the foot of Cap d'Antibes, shallow and close to old Antibes. The tourist office describes it with lifeguard posts, toilets and showers, and a Handi-plage point near the water sports centre.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Neither the town hall of Antibes Juan-les-Pins nor the tourist office publishes a rule saying dogs are admitted on this beach, and several unofficial guides claim on the contrary that Antibes beaches are off-limits to dogs in summer, with uncertain tolerance out of season. We found no order that settles the question: call the town hall before coming with your dog, especially from June to September, when the beach is supervised from 9am to 7pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if in doubt, favour the Cap d'Antibes coastal path, a stone's throw away, for a walk with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Old Antibes and its Provençal market are a few minutes away, as is the coastal path along Cap d'Antibes.</p>
